# The full container run at a04e91a7: 33 gates, 31 593 tests, nothing failed (2026-10-04)

`scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --full` was run end to end against the committed tree at
`a04e91a7` and passed: 33 gates, 386 test-result blocks, 31 593 tests passed, 485 ignored,
0 failed, exit 0. This log records the verdict lines, the size of each leg, the two fixtures
that skipped inside the container and why, and what the run does not cover. It is the
counterpart to `docs/verification/verify-in-docker-frozen-6b8b3dad-2026-10-03.log`, which
covered the previous commit; the numbers moved because gates and tests were added since.

The full 3.0 MB / 35 869-line transcript is not committed. Every line quoted below is copied
out of it, and section 6 gives the commands to reproduce it and to re-measure the counts.

== 0. Why the run sits in its own clone

`scripts/verify-in-docker.sh` bind-mounts the repository root it was invoked from, and it
fingerprints the working tree once before the gates and once after; on any movement it prints
`UNATTRIBUTABLE: the source tree changed while the gates ran.` and exits 1. Running it in the
live checkout would have meant a 25-minute verdict attributed to a tree that was being edited
throughout, so the run went to a self-contained clone:

    $ git clone <this repository> /var/tmp/verify-frozen-a04e91a7
    $ cd /var/tmp/verify-frozen-a04e91a7 && git checkout --detach a04e91a7
    HEAD is now at a04e91a7 feat(ci): metric 调用的数组多一个值就当场 abort，编译器与 panic 普查都看不见它
    $ IMAGE_TAG=chaos-verify:frozen ./scripts/verify-in-docker.sh --full \
          > /var/tmp/verify-full-a04e91a7.log 2>&1; echo "DOCKER-FULL-EXIT=$?" \
          > /var/tmp/verify-full-a04e91a7.exit

`git worktree` is not an option here: the script's first action is a preflight in which the
container reads the mounted `/src` with git, and a worktree's `.git` is a text pointer to a
file inside the parent repository that does not exist inside the container, so the preflight
refuses the tree. A clone carries its own object store, so the preflight passes.

`--detach` pins the tree to that one commit rather than to a branch head. The clone's
`git status --porcelain` was empty before the run and is empty now, which is what makes the
checksum below a claim about `a04e91a7` and not about a working state.

== 1. The verdict, as printed

    == building chaos-verify:frozen from docker.io/library/debian:bookworm-slim
    == preparing cargo cache volumes
    == source tree: 3996 files, checksum 4160701699

    == preflight: container can read the repository
    preflight: OK

    == toolchain matches the pin
    rustc 1.94.0 (4a4ef493e 2026-03-02)
    cargo 1.94.0 (85eff7c80 2026-01-15)

    == pinned protoc launcher
    libprotoc 29.3

    ...

    all gates passed in chaos-verify:frozen

and the exit code, from the `echo` appended to the command rather than from the script:

    $ cat /var/tmp/verify-full-a04e91a7.exit
    DOCKER-FULL-EXIT=0

The run did not print `UNATTRIBUTABLE`. The script recomputes the same checksum after the last
gate and prints that sentence only on a mismatch, so its absence is the statement that all 33
gates, and the 31 593 tests inside them, belong to the tree whose checksum is 4160701699 and
that no file moved while they ran.

Elapsed time was 1 521 seconds (25 minutes 21 seconds), from the transcript's creation to its
last write. That is not a cold-cache figure: the cargo registry, the cargo git checkouts and
`target/` live in three named volumes (`chaos-verify-cargo-registry`,
`chaos-verify-cargo-git`, `chaos-verify-target`) that earlier runs had already filled, and the
image layers were reused. `IMAGE_TAG=chaos-verify:frozen` only renames the build. On a clean
machine the same command takes considerably longer, and 25 minutes should not be read as a
baseline.

== 2. What ran

`scripts/verify-gates.sh --list` in that clone prints 33 gate names, which is the `gates=()`
