The host-side runner is a subset of the same array: `bash scripts/verify-gates.sh` on this
machine skips the four legs that need the container toolchain (`cargo check`, `cargo clippy`,
`cargo test`, `GUI protocol types`) and runs the other 29. The container is the only place all
33 are executed, which is the reason for doing this at all rather than trusting the host sweep.

Three gates print a count worth recording, because they are the ones that read the whole tree:

